<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>AlgMap-15.8</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the equation \[ {@ex@} = 0 \] by completing the square. Give exact answers.</p>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Write the left-hand side in the form \(a(x+p)^2+q\).</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] \(= 0\) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Hence give both solutions as a set. Type <code>sqrt(5)</code> for \(\sqrt{5}\).</p>
<div>\(x \in \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>When the coefficient of \(x^2\) is not 1, first <strong>divide through by it</strong> (or take it out as a factor), then complete the square on \(x^2 + \frac{b}{a}x\) as usual.</p>
<p><strong>Step 1.</strong> Take out the factor \({@aa@}\) from the two terms in \(x\): \({@aa*x^2+bb*x@} = {@aa@}\left({@x^2+bb/aa*x@}\right)\). The constant term \({@cc@}\) is dealt with at the end.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2.</strong> Half the coefficient of \(x\) inside the bracket is \({@hh@}\), so \({@x^2+bb/aa*x@} = {@(x+hh)^2@} - {@hh^2@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 3.</strong> Multiply back by \({@aa@}\) and collect the constants. Note that the \(-{@hh^2@}\) is multiplied by \({@aa@}\) too:</p>
\[ {@aa@}\left({@(x+hh)^2@} - {@hh^2@}\right) = {@aa*(x+hh)^2@} - {@aa*hh^2@}, \]
<p>and adding the constant term \({@cc@}\) gives \({@ex@} = {@cta@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 4.</strong> Set it equal to zero and rearrange: \({@(x+hh)^2@} = {@-qq/aa@}\).</p>
<p><strong>Step 5.</strong> Take square roots (\(\pm\)) and solve: \({@x+hh@} = \pm {@sqrt(-qq/aa)@}\), so</p>
\[ x = {@ta1@} \quad\text{or}\quad x = {@ta2@}. \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
